-- Backfill the mid-article branded CTA on every published post.
--
-- One offer per topic cluster rather than a bespoke card per post: the point of
-- the block is that a dubbing article sells a dub instead of a generic "sign
-- up", and seven offers already cover the blog. Wording lives per cluster so it
-- stays editable in one place; an admin can override any single post from the
-- dashboard afterwards, which is the reason this is a column and not a constant.
--
-- Every number here is checkable in the codebase, because a CTA promising
-- something the product does not do converts once and refunds forever:
--   60s free dub    -> STARTER_MAX_DUB_SECONDS (packages/validations/src/consts/dubbing.ts)
--   29 languages    -> the dubbing dashboard copy
--   5 thumbnails    -> generateCount max (packages/validations/src/schema/thumbnail.schema.ts)
--   10 video ideas  -> IDEATION_ABSOLUTE_MAX_IDEAS (packages/validations/src/consts/ideation.ts)
--   500 credits/mo  -> 20260716000000_starter_credits_500.sql
--
-- Replayable: matches on slug and writes only branded_cta, so re-running it
-- restores the seeded copy without touching any other column.
--
-- Cluster counts: dubbing 6, generic 10, ideas 5, retention 2, scripts 12, subtitles 8, thumbnails 5.

UPDATE public.blog_posts AS b
SET branded_cta = s.branded_cta,
    updated_at  = now()
